## Interface: 11509, 20506, 16001
## AllowLoadGameType: vanilla, tbc, camelot
## Title: ZacUI |cff33ff99Raid mods|r
## Notes: Boss mods for the Classic Era raids (Molten Core to Naxxramas) and, on TBC, Karazhan to the Sunwell, as part of ZacUI: timers, warnings, icons, lists, raid frame and nameplate marks, driven by the combat log. ZacUI's own code - no aura engine needed.
## Author: Zac
## Version: 3.0.9
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\ZacUI\Media\addonIcon
## X-Category: Interface Enhancements
## Dependencies: Zacui, Zacui_RaidTools
## OptionalDeps: Zacui_UnitFrames, Zacui_Nameplates, LibSharedMedia-3.0, LibRangeCheck-3.0
## X-ZacUI-Part: Raid mods

# Part of ZacUI. It shares ZacUI's namespace (_G.ZacUI, published by
# Core_Boot) and its saved variables; its settings live in ZacUIDB.raidmods.
#
# Zacui_RaidTools is required for the globals and slash commands the
# modules call (/pull, /break, /range, the speech settings, the raid
# sync), and it carries LibSharedMedia. The unit frames and nameplates
# are optional: the marks that ride on them simply have nowhere to go
# without them.
#
# Sounds are the game's own: callouts are spoken with text-to-speech
# ("tts:..."), alerts are the game's interface sounds ("ui:..."), see
# Zacui\Core\Core_Sounds.lua. Media\Own\ holds ZacUI's own shapes
# (rings, circles, glows, the Thaddius arrow). Libs\ carries the
# aura engine's LibCustomGlow (the real pixel / autocast glows) and
# LibRangeCheck (one range check the MC pack makes), so neither depends
# on the aura engine being enabled.

# LIBRARIES (LibStub keeps the first copy loaded)
Libs\LibStub.lua
Libs\CallbackHandler-1.0.lua
Libs\LibRangeCheck-3.0.lua
Libs\LibCustomGlow-1.0.lua

# THE ENGINE
RM_Core.lua
RM_Triggers.lua
RM_Widgets.lua
RM_Anchors.lua
RM_Config.lua
# hand-written helpers on top of the packs (Razuvious on you)
RM_Extras.lua

# How a raid module is put together, and the behaviours they share
RM_Own.lua
RM_OwnKit.lua

